+# AGENTS.md
+
+## NCG Hosting and Network: Read-Only by Default
+
+For NCG infrastructure analysis, production `10.1.0.0/16` and development `10.0.0.0/16` are read-only. This also covers their hosts, containers, databases, registry, CI/CD and network management through public URLs or other access paths. Full Access, VPN connectivity, available credentials and documented commands are not authorization to change these systems.
+
+Read-only inspection needs no per-command confirmation. Any write or system-changing operation requires Daniel's explicit prior approval for the concrete target and action, including changes initiated indirectly through pipelines, APIs, scripts or remote Docker contexts. Inspect helpers before execution; if side effects are unclear, stop and ask. No automatic fixes, remote temporary files, installs, pulls, restarts, deployments, migrations or active security tests under an analysis-only instruction. Existing build/deploy/test examples below do not override this restriction. Authorized local documentation and protected local evidence writes remain allowed.
+
+Before remote audit work, read the [NCG read-only audit policy](/Users/dh/Documents/DanielsVault/ncg/ncg-docs/docs/Ops/Security/NCG-Audit-Read-Only-Policy.md). Pass this restriction to any delegated work. It remains in force across audit continuations unless Daniel explicitly changes it; approval of one action does not lift the general restriction.
+
+## Project Orientation
+`ncg-backend` is a .NET microservice backend for the Nagel Car Group e-commerce webshop: [auto-nagel.de/shop](https://www.auto-nagel.de/shop/).
+
+When starting work in this repository, read `README.md` first for current runtime architecture, then read the repo spec documents under `backend/sources/specs` before changing behavior:
+- `README.md`
+- `backend/AGENTS.md` for git-root workflow and completion guidance
+- `backend/sources/README.md` when touching runtime architecture, services, or commands
+- `backend/sources/AGENTS.md` for command routing and machine-oriented context
+- `backend/sources/SERVICES_INVENTORY.md` when changing service wiring or dependencies
+- `backend/sources/secrets/README.md` when touching local secrets, STS credentials, or F5 config
+- `backend/sources/tests/README.md` for check-build, incident tooling, and targeted runtime gates
+- `backend/sources/Makefile` and `backend/sources/tests/resilience/` when touching mocked-neighbor resilience verification or observability evidence
+- `backend/.gitlab/scripts/README.md` when touching CI build/deploy/check-build orchestration
+- `backend/sources/tests/secrets-validation/README.md` when validating local Docker secret wiring
+- relevant specs under `backend/sources/specs/*.md`
+- active change files under `backend/sources/specs/changes/<change-id>/`
+- active change `proposal.md`, `implementation-evidence.md`, `acceptance-criteria-matrix.md`, and `tasks.md` only when more context is needed
+- past change `proposal.md`, `implementation-evidence.md`, and acceptance criteria if a new spec conflicts with old work
+
+Do not treat implementation code as the only source of truth. Requirements and rollout evidence belong in the repo spec/change documents.
+
+## Multi-Repository NCG Project
+This file is also the primary guidance for the local Codex project `ncg`. That project attaches these related repositories:
+
+- Backend: `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG/ncg-backend/backend`
+- Frontend: `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG/ncg-frontend`
+- Security Token Service: `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG/ncg-security-token`
+- Pimcore: `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG/pimcore`
+- Operations and architecture documentation: `/Users/dh/Documents/DanielsVault/ncg/ncg-docs`
+
+When a task may span repositories:
+
+1. State which repositories are in scope before editing and leave the others untouched.
+2. Read each in-scope repository's own `AGENTS.md`, `README.md`, and requirement/spec source before changing it. Codex does not automatically discover project guidance in secondary project folders.
+3. Run `git status --short` from every actual Git root in scope. Never treat `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG` or `/Users/dh/Documents/Dev/NCG/ncg-backend` as a shared Git root.
+4. Establish the shared contract, dependency order, and rollout sequence before implementation. Record behavioral requirements in the repository that owns them; update `ncg-docs` when cross-service architecture or operational contracts change.
+5. Treat repositories as independent delivery units with their own branches, commits, pull requests, tests, and rollback boundaries. A worktree for the primary repository does not isolate changes in attached secondary repositories.
+6. Verify each changed repository through its prescribed checks, then verify the cross-repository behavior at the most direct available end-to-end boundary. Report exactly which repositories and verification levels were covered.
