+## Do / Don't Rules
+Do:
+- Work from `backend/sources` for build/test/runtime commands.
+- Follow .NET naming conventions: `PascalCase` for types/methods, `camelCase` for locals/parameters.
+- Keep controllers thin; place business logic in service/domain layers.
+- Use the `$tdd` skill for feature and bug work (failing behavior test first).
+- Use existing stack first: .NET 9, EF Core, Ocelot, Polly, Serilog/Sentry.
+- Use `backend/sources/specs/changes/<change-id>/tasks.md` as the resumable work log for meaningful behavior changes.
