+For deployment/runtime incidents, use the check-build tooling described in `backend/sources/tests/README.md`. The manual local flow is pull artifact -> analyze incident bundle -> generate plan; the watcher flow can arm the next branch build and then run that chain automatically.
+The remote collector chain behind those workflows is `bash tests/check-build.sh` -> `warmup.sh` + `observe.sh` -> `diagnose.sh`; use `backend/sources/tests/README.md` for the expected incident bundle contents and failure semantics.
+For mocked neighbor degradation verification, use `backend/sources/Makefile` or `backend/sources/tests/resilience/verify-neighbor-resilience.sh`; the harness layers `docker-compose.resilience.yml` over `docker-compose.local.yml` and writes evidence to `tests/resilience/artifacts/result.json`, `result.junit.xml`, and `resilience-compose.log`.
